From e786a898bde751aafc03f13c175cabe842cf4e08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:55:45 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] build: one reproducible firmware from Make and Meson

Meson's default buildtype is debug (-O0 -g), so a plain `meson setup` built
different firmware from the Makefile (-O2), which is what was tested on
hardware. Distributions only got matching images because they pass
-Doptimization=2 -Ddebug=false themselves.

Make optimization=2 and debug=false the project defaults. With them, Meson
and the Makefile produce byte-identical images for all seven variants with
the same Clang/LLD. Add tests/check-reproducible.sh, which builds both and
compares every image, and run it in CI. The docs no longer suggest
--buildtype=release (-O3), and they now say that injected CFLAGS change the
code.

Tested on the arm64 buildbox with clang 22.1.6: check-reproducible reports all
seven images identical. Their hashes are those of the images that ran on the
J616s and the M2 on 2026-11-01.
[dylan: one co-author trailer of the original message is not reproduced here]

